			"Message": "fix(Project): Supply missing INativeWindowConfiguration fields in sandbox config and refresh doc diagrams\n\nAdd eight non-optional fields to Mountain's `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` JSON blob that VS Code's environment service layers access without null-checks: `perfMarks`, `loggers`, `colorScheme`, `mainPid`, `os` (release/hostname/arch), `dataFolderName`/`sharedDataFolderName` (defaulting to `.fiddee`), and `version`. Missing any of these causes a `TypeError` during extension host initialization and workbench service construction, crashing startup.\n\nIn Maintain, rewrite the Mermaid architecture diagram in README.md to document internal modules (Build CLI, Rhai scripting, Run logic), shell entrypoints (Debug/Release builds, SignBundle, BrotliPrebake), and build artifacts with color-coded classDefs. Also fix a literal tab character in PlistEdit.rs, replacing it with the escaped byte `\\t`.\n\nCocoon's Target artifacts are rebuilt and RouteManifest timestamp synchronized — no source-level changes, confirming the build pipeline consistency.\n\nThese changes prevent extension host startup crashes, improve developer documentation of the build system, and keep compiled artifacts aligned with source revisions.",
			"SHA": "b3e613bae60945dd1c50477d68489fc303e393ee"
		}
